\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  The day is past and over
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj  All thanks, O Lord, to Thee
\par  I pray Thee now that sinless
\par  The hours of dark may be
\par  O Jesus, keep me in Thy sight
\par  And guard me through the coming night
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  The joys of day are over
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj  I lift my heart to Thee
\par  And pray Thee that offenceless
\par  The hours of dark may be
\par  O Jesus, keep me in Thy sight
\par  And guard me through the coming night.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  The toils of day are over
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 I raise the hymn to Thee
\par And pray that free from peril
\par The hours of dark maybe
\par O Jesus, keep me in Thy sight
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj And guard me through the coming night
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  Be Thou my soul's Preserver
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 O God, for Thou dost know
\par How many are the perils
\par Through which I have to go
\par Lover of men, O hear my call
\par \pard      And guard and save me from them all.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

